            <ArticleTitle>Gastric trichobezoar.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1907</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/ccr3.1213</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Trichobezoar is a rare gastrointestinal pathology, but should be considered in patients with abdominal mass and previous history of trichophagia. In physical examination, it is important to verify signs of alopecia. Minimally invasive surgery is a secure method to remove the specimen from the stomach.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
